// Dialog :
"P2622769564" "As a favor for the Hetman, you drove away the D.U.S.T. cell that had taken up camp near the Compound. Now he owes you an audience with the Monarch."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3453998670" "Report your success to the Hetman"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P328448929" "{HeroName}, you done good, very good. Only it's not me you should be braggin' it to, ya know. Tell the Hetman of the Compound. Getting' on his good side means we're closer to getting' my folk outta the mess they're in."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccessFlashback 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P315940796" "The Hetman has reluctantly agreed to let you speak to the Monarch about the Carnival captives. He's warned you, though, that the Monarch is a bit touched in the head, convinced that his imaginary daughter has been kidnapped."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3339937000" "Convince the Monarch to let you speak to the imprisoned Carnival members"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3164098399" "Here's our chance, {Hero.gender=male boy|girl}!The Monarch might be crazy, but he's the only one that can free my peoples. Well, war could, too, ya know, but none of us wants that yet."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccessFlashback 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4155131012" "The only way you could get the Monarch's permission to speak to the Carnival prisoners was to agree to help him find his daughter, 'Anna'. He gave you a watercolor portrait of her, saying it would help your search. Everyone in the Compound that knows the Monarch well swears he never had a daughter. To pull this off, you're going to need to get lucky or clever; hopefully, both at once."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part8 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1187167273" "Speak to the Carnival Prisoner, Candlestick"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P679046894" "Lissen here, {HeroName}, you a'wastin' time talking to me. Talk to one of the Carnival troupers an' see if there ain't some way to reconcile with the Compound."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3453100186" "When you showed the watercolor portrait of Anna to Candlestick, his psychic powers confirmed that she was indeed a real person. He could sense her presence in First Ward, but that was all. Mistress Nadia's magic, however, may be able to pinpoint an exact location."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBeginFlashback 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskAbandon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3120713084" "So now, child, what have we here..? An imaginary daughter who turns out to be a real live girl, eh? Mistress Nadia's feelin' a crazy quilt comin' our way, you can bet on that. Hand me that portrait the Monarch painted of his daughter and let's see if I can't scry where she might be hidin', hm? Usually the mojo go doubletime with a link like this one, so personal, an' made by hand, an' all caught up in sorrow.<br><br><color orange>Lemme know when you're ready to find Little Miss Watercolor here.</color> My peoples in the Carnival aren't out of danger yet, y'know."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TaggartDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P2647847186" "Hold on, now! You're from the PPD, right? I've got no beef with you...well, I <i>did</i> but that was back Coleside. S'what got me shipped to the Ward in the first place.<br><br>Or maybe you're not a cop, I don't really care, just hear me out--"
// Answer Text :
"P224749943" "Tell me where she is. (Show Taggart the portrait of Anna)"
// Page WhereIsShe Text :
"P1858939457" "You've gotta be kidding me. You saw that <color red>Shepherd</color> group attacking my operation, right? You couldn't have missed it.<br><br>Who do you think <i>runs</i> that group? She ain't here with 'em today, but she sure did send 'em. You can probably find her at their <color yellow>Haven</color>, a defunct warehouse due east of here, skirting the Free-Fire Zone."
// Answer Text :
"P170675360" "You could've made this easier on yourself, Taggart."
// Page ShuttingYouDown Text :
"P4229280079" "Lookee here, we got us a mudbelly with <i>conflictin' principles</i>..! Kinda like them high-horse Shepherds out there wreckin' the joint. Only thing is, you <i>do</i> know, even if you go through me, they're not going to play nice with you when you go looking for their leader, {Hero.gender=male boy|girlie}, right?"
// Answer Text :
"P3575497488" "I'll take my chances."
// Page TakeMyChances Text :
"P180090402" "<color orange>Taggart collapses from his wounds</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - AnnaDialogTree1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P1519828486" "Hold! I will surrender...to whatever foulness you work for--<br><br>Who was it? Taggart? D.U.S.T.? Who sent you?"
// Answer Text :
"P3266959033" "Taggart? You mean the slavemaster? I shut his operation down. (optional)"
// Answer Text :
"P760915304" "Calm down, Anna. Your father sent me."
// Answer Text :
"P1133627768" "(Show Anna the watercolor portrait)"
// Page ShutDownTaggartPage Text :
"P3046063127" "You...did? Why?"
// Answer Text :
"P770558081" "I suspect for the same reasons your crazed, violence-prone cult was trying it."
// Page PortraitPage1 Text :
"P1001520265" "<color orange>You show Anna the watercolor portrait that the Monarch painted. The effects of the image move from a disconcerting sense of loss to a slowly rising anger.</color><br><br>Is this some kind of sick joke? Which twisted faction in all of First Ward do you represent?<br><br><i>I command you to tell me who sent you!</i>"
// Answer Text :
"P3551304622" "Relax. I share no allegiance with your enemies, especially Taggart. I shut his operation down."
// Page YourCultPage Text :
"P4142451502" "We are <i>not</i>  a cult. We're just...no, you're right. These particular Shepherds like to think themselves as one. But you judge them too harshly. Crazed and violent? That describes most First Warders.<br><br>I have been trying to change that, to redirect their purposes. Towards something better than merely recovering through magical artifacts from the Carnival's trash bins. It's just been...taking awhile. And you: tell me now of your purpose. Why have you come?"
// Answer Text :
"P287738449" "Your father sent me."
// Page FatherRevealPage1 Text :
"P4062510514" "Tread carefully when speaking of my father. He is long dead. And his passing was unkind in its circumstances."
// Answer Text :
"P3205950474" "No, he's waiting for you at the Compound...Antebellum."
// Page AntebellumPage Text :
"P4241827888" "How...how do you know that name? My father called me that when I was only a child."
// Answer Text :
"P1456516518" "When your best friend in the whole world was a tireless bike, I know. He's alive, Anna."
// Page ReallyAlivePage1 Text :
"P3486794881" "My father is dead, {HeroName}, of that I am sure. How you or he came to know these things of me, though, I do not know, and would have answers. <color orange>I will meet with this Monarch. I have affairs to settle with the Shepherds here first, but I will be at the Compound when you return to it.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2218980890" "I'll see you at the Compound."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MonarchDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2937999289" "I am dying, {HeroName}, and these are my last wishes. It may seem quite mad to you-- and it will seem so to the others of the Compound, but they have known me long that way these days--but tell Anna that she is my Palatine. The Throne of the Compound will pass to her now."
// Answer Text :
"P2400508821" "You're doing this because you still have fragments of her as your daughter in your memory."
// Page FragmentPage Text :
"P3608451180" "Of course I do. I played host to that <color red>Apparition<color> for so...<i>long</i>. To look on her is to feel a loss I cannot reconcile with my <i>own</i> memories. But she is strong and forthright and dear to me still, even without ties of blood. She will be a better leader for the Compound than I have ever been."
// Answer Text :
"P514828341" "I have a feeling that the Hetman will not like your last command."
// Page MonarchDiesPage Text :
"P2117337697" "Then I make one more: <i>you</i> will find a way to enforce it."
// Answer Text :
"P2141117208" "Leave."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - AnnaDoorDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page ReadyNow Text :
"P3662785928" "Are you ready yet?"
// Answer Text :
"P1408420321" "Let's go (Start Mission)"
// Answer Text :
"P1250495012" "Not yet (Leave)"
// Page StaringAtMe Text :
"P3724406499" "They're staring at me, {HeroName}. And not with the normal unease reserved for a Shepherd, but with a...with a..."
// Answer Text :
"P1036354826" "Of recognition, Anna. They've seen the Monarch's paintings. They know you're his daughter."
// Page TheyKnow Text :
"P2784068058" "If you must know, my father died in the <color red>Asylum</color> shortly after the Emperor sent us to First Ward. He went insane from the iniquities he found here and shortly after that the seers dragged him away. Orphaned in the ruins, I went native.<br><br>Whoever you're taking me to <b>isn't</b> my father, but I can see that some part of you wants him to be. And I choose to believe that's born out of compassion and not some baser agenda. Whatever the case, <b>no one</b> escapes the Asylum,  {HeroName}. This is either a trap or the prologue to something far more sinister. You would do good to prepare yourself for what happens next."
// Answer Text :
"P3678658405" "I've worked hard to get you here, Anna. We can do this."
// Answer Text :
"P3920331125" "Calvin Scott escaped from the Asylum, you know. (optional)"
// Page CalvinScottPage Text :
"P1007850820" "I stand corrected. The famous Calvin Scott seems to be the exception to every rule."
// Page WeCanDoThis Text :
"P2824102101" "Let's get it over with, then."
// Answer Text :
"P843154088" "We'll be fine (Start Mission)"
// Answer Text :
"P4050590189" "I'm not ready yet, give me a second (Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P480377803" "Hmm, this picture has some <i>strong</i>  power in it, {Hero.gender=male boy|girl}..! Whatever the rest of the gumbo thinks, the loas are tellin' me that this definitely ties blood to blood, they're just not sure how. Perhaps the Monarch's not off his rocker, after all.<br><br>The loas <i>also</i>  say that our Watercolor moves around a bunch. I'm seeing a <color red>slaver den</color>, but I'm not sure if she's there now or not. In any case, she <b>has</b> been there, so that's your first step. <color orange>Go to the slaver den and find out what you can.</color> Its operation is run by a <color red>Dreg</color> with mighty-high notions of himself called <color red>Taggart.</color> <color orange>Make sure to show he and his peoples that the Compound is protected.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P2501211814" "I'll look for her there."
// SendOffString :
"P1364588949" "Make the spirits proud, {HeroName}. <color orange>And be sure to question any slaves you find in that den, too.</color> The more we know of the watercolor girl, the easier the loas can help bring her home."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3633446256" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: Thou Shalt in Thy Daughter See</color>"

